# ── Supabase ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in the two values from
# Supabase → Project Settings → Data API (and → API Keys for the key).
#
# Both are NEXT_PUBLIC_ because the browser needs them: the anon key
# identifies the project, it does not grant anything. What a request may
# read or write is decided by the row-level policies in
# supabase/schema.sql against the signed-in session, so this key sitting
# in the page source is no more revealing than the URL beside it.
#
# There is deliberately no service-role key here. That key bypasses every
# policy, and nothing in this app needs it — the admin writes go through
# the organiser's own session. Never put it in a NEXT_PUBLIC_ variable.

NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key
